# UI / UX rules

- Visual direction: **cartoon pirate excursion first** — animated fleet, warm storybook seas,
  islands, charts, timber and sails. Concentrate neon/casino language in loot-box/jackpot
  ceremonies and selected high-stakes peaks. Never make it an admin dashboard.
- Mobile-first, portrait-friendly, iPhone-native feel. Max content width ~28rem, big
  tap targets (min 52px), readable text, strong contrast.
- The UI teaches the game: short labels, icons, and animated sequencing instead of rules pages.
- Animations (Framer Motion + Tailwind keyframes) must clarify game events, not hide them.
  Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (global fallback lives in `styles/index.css`).
- Never rely on colour alone for meaning — pair with authored symbols/text/state shapes.
- Timers must always be visible during timed phases (`TimerBar` fed by server `timerEndsAt`).
- Private information (mutiny, clues, inventory effects) must be clearly marked private.
- Score changes only appear through the reveal queue (`RevealScreen`) or animated counters —
  never teleport numbers silently.
- Microcopy follows the 3 C's (clarity > concision > character): every label is as short as
  possible, buttons name the outcome ("Place Bet", "Start Game" — never "Submit"), and each
  screen asks the player for exactly ONE decision (Jackbox pacing principle).
- Pirate flavour is welcome ("MUTINY!", "Fool's Gold") but never at the cost of clarity —
  flavour lives in reveals and titles, instructions stay plain. Keep it 9+ friendly.
- Round rules are taught by the intro screen in max 3 short bullets; everything else is
  learned by playing (progressive disclosure). No walls of text, ever.
- Follow `docs/context/VISUAL_DIRECTION.md` and `docs/context/ANIMATION_AND_ASSETS.md`.
